        "summary": "Diff body to a base..head range, spec and task specs to paths, --stat to --numstat --no-renames -z. Deleting the payload deletes what existed to make it fit: three cursor fitters, the ratchet char budget, the 50 KB cap, eight argv constants, the three 'truncated to fit' markers, and both impl prompt builders whose only difference was fitting.",
        "taskIds": [
          "fn-169-review-subsystem-agentic-first-pass.4"
        ],
        "title": "Payloads become identities, and the fitting layer is deleted"
      },
      {
        "files": [],
        "kind": "step",
        "ordinal": 6,
        "rIds": [
          "R3"
        ],
        "sourceRefs": [
          "spec",
          "rid-R3",
          "task-4"
        ],
        "summary": "The model rests on the changed-file list being complete, and git abbreviates three independent ways: --stat elides with an ellipsis (28 of 43 paths on this spec's own diff), plain --numstat collapses renames to brace notation, and without -z any non-ASCII path is C-quoted. All three were found by running the real command; two of them by the reviewer.",
        "taskIds": [
          "fn-169-review-subsystem-agentic-first-pass.4"
        ],
        "title": "Make the scope map actually resolvable"
      },
      {
        "files": [],
        "kind": "step",
        "ordinal": 7,
        "rIds": [
          "R3"
        ],
        "sourceRefs": [
          "spec",
          "rid-R3",
          "task-4"
        ],
        "summary": "A failed git read raises with git's own message and aborts before a round is reserved; a genuinely empty range still returns empty. The artifact identity is the complete diff at the frozen range, streamed under a ceiling that raises rather than truncating, because a truncated identity collides with any diff sharing its prefix. A task with no readable markdown aborts instead of being invisible to both prompt and hash.",
        "taskIds": [
          "fn-169-review-subsystem-agentic-first-pass.4"
        ],
        "title": "Fail loudly where silence used to degrade the review"
      },
