    "thesis": "Review prompts stop shipping the reviewer bytes it can fetch itself. A review now carries a commit range, the exact changed-path list, and spec/task paths; the reviewer reads the rest from the checkout. That deletes the layer built to make the payload fit, and closes the false-SHIP hole where a truncated prompt let an honest all-clear cover findings the reviewer never saw."
